    "workDescription": "The Safety Manager for the 203rd RED HORSE Squadron (203 RHS) serves as the primary technical advisor to the squadron commander on occupational and construction safety programs, operating out of the Safety Office located in the HQ Bld 203 in Room 108. Tasked with overseeing high-risk heavy engineering missions in both garrison and austere environments, the Safety Manager conducts site inspections for complex projects like rapid airfield repair and vertical construction, performs Job Hazard Analyses (JHA), and leads mishap investigations. They ensure the unit remains deployment-ready by integrating Operational Risk Management (ORM) into mission planning, overseeing heavy equipment safety protocols, and enforcing strict compliance with DAFMAN 91-203 and OSHA construction standards to mitigate the loss of personnel and equipment during critical engineering operations.",
